mod_audio_fork: guard NULL argv dereferences on the uuid_audio_fork start path.

1. "uuid_audio_fork <uuid> start <url> <mix>" (no sampling-rate token) called strcmp(argv[4])
   with argv[4] == NULL and crashed FreeSWITCH. The sampling rate is now parsed only when present;
   the existing default of 8000 is kept. Every invocation with a sampling-rate token is unchanged.
2. The usage guard compared argv[1] case-sensitively while dispatch uses strcasecmp, so "START"
   with fewer than 4 tokens bypassed the guard and dereferenced a NULL URL/mix. The guard now uses
   strcasecmp as well; such commands return -USAGE.
3. A start command whose URL failed to parse, or whose sampling rate was not a positive multiple of
   8000 up to 64000, was logged as invalid and then started anyway: start_capture ran with an
   uninitialised host/path/port, and a negative or overflowing rate sized the frame buffer from a
   negative length (std::bad_alloc through C frames, SIGABRT). start_capture now runs only when
   both are valid; otherwise the command returns -ERR. Valid commands are unchanged.
4. A websocket URL of MAX_WS_URL_LEN (512) bytes or more is refused before parse_ws_uri: that
   function copies up to 4608 bytes into its stack buffer and the host into a 512-byte buffer with
   strncpy, which leaves both unterminated for long input, and runs std::regex over the whole URL.
   The bridge's URL is about 70 bytes.

Against drachtio-freeswitch-modules 88e1465908a89bed5c95d336aa53a3899bb5abb5, modules/mod_audio_fork.
Apply from the module directory: patch -p1 --forward --fuzz=0 --batch
